menuconfig MODULES_HOLD_RIG_ATT
	bool "hold_rig_att"
	default n
	---help---
		Enable support for hold_rig_att

		Standalone, manually-started controller that ramps the vehicle
		to an arbitrary commanded 3D attitude and holds it there, for a
		fixture that physically prevents translation (e.g. a 3-axis
		gimbal/gyroscope test rig). Driven through the ATTITUDE setpoint
		path (mc_att_control) instead of raw body rates. The
		standing-still counterpart to flip_rig_axis: that module rotates
		through a revolution about a fixed axis, this one travels to one
		orientation and parks on it.

		The target is specified either as a tilt magnitude plus a tilt
		direction (HRATT_MODE 0, degenerate nowhere in 0-180 degrees) or
		as Euler roll and pitch (HRATT_MODE 1, which loses control of
		tilt near 90 degrees because Z-Y-X applies pitch about the
		already-rolled axis). Ramping rather than stepping is what makes
		large angles safe: a static setpoint saturates MC_ROLLRATE_MAX
		past only ~57 degrees of error.

		Never touches position/GPS - start with `hold_rig_att start` and
		do not run it alongside another OFFBOARD-publishing module.
		Requires FD_FAIL_R/FD_FAIL_P to be relaxed for holds past 60
		degrees; the module warns about that and several other failsafes
		at startup.
